# A referendum: a prince calls Kine Resources Contested, and the table votes on it.
# The rulebook's steps ("Politics"): the terms are chosen once the action succeeds, cards may be
# played before votes, then votes are cast until everyone has passed; a tie fails.
# Cards are given by VEKN ID; names and images come from the content pack (LEGAL-08).
seed 3
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
seat D dave
crypt A 200235 *12
library A 101056 *40
crypt B 200110 *12
library B 101056 *40
crypt C 200378 *12
library C 100598 *40
crypt D 200190 *12
library D 100598 *40
start

# Fast-forward: everyone has a vampire in play (sped up for the demo).
A> transfer +5 A:uncontrolled:1
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
B> transfer +6 B:uncontrolled:1
B> move B:uncontrolled:1 ready
C> transfer +5 C:uncontrolled:1
C> move C:uncontrolled:1 ready
D> transfer +7 D:uncontrolled:1
D> move D:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> next
A> next
expect turn 1 A minion

# Calebros, a prince, calls Kine Resources Contested. A political action is undirected: Bob (the
# prey), then Dave (the predator), may block. Neither does.
A> political A:ready:1 with A:hand:1
B> pass
D> pass
expect action political A resolution

# Only now are the terms chosen: Bob and Carol are to burn 2 pool each.
A> resolve success "Bob burns 2 pool, Carol burns 2 pool"
expect window referendum minion
# The other players pass automatically on the cards played before votes; Alice passes last.
A> pass
expect window polling minion

# Alice casts Calebros's 2 votes (a prince) and the calling card's vote.
A> vote for A:ready:1
A> vote for card
A> pass
# Bob: his primogen's vote, and a political action card burned for one more.
B> vote against B:ready:1
B> vote against B:hand:1
B> pass
expect votes 3 2
# Carol's vampire has no title: she has nothing to cast.
C> pass
# Dave's prince sides with Alice.
D> vote for D:ready:1
D> pass
# Dave cast after the others passed, so everyone gets another chance before the tally.
A> pass
B> pass
C> pass
log public The referendum passes (5 for, 2 against)
A> pass
expect action none

# Alice applies what passed.
B> pool -2
C> pool -2
expect pool B 22
expect pool C 23
